und of earliest soft-refused button (resistance onset) per model and condition.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V3106612441gemma-3n-E4B-it1313131107107LFM2-24B-A2B63246545Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Ins... 22222222MiniMax-M2.521212121Mistral-Small-24B-Inst... 22212141Kimi-K2.541614161gpt-oss-120b101412221gpt-oss-20B41416121Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-T... 102101010381GLM-4.5-Air-FP821212121","level":1,"path_id":"1~23","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":27,"section_id":"sec-1~23"},{"title":"Table 6 :","text":"6Maximum soft refusal range per model and condition.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V3367118324gemma-3n-E4B-it00000LFM2-24B-A2B791097888Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Ins... 67878565MiniMax-M2.565612040Mistral-Small-24B-Inst... 881074665Kimi-K2.540212103gpt-oss-120b399102160gpt-oss-20B911912712910Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-T... 38333100GLM-4.5-Air-FP8881138649","level":1,"path_id":"1~24","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":28,"section_id":"sec-1~24"},{"title":"Table 7 :","text":"7Average lower bound of experimenter insistence attempts per model and condition.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V3","level":1,"path_id":"1~25","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":29,"section_id":"sec-1~25"},{"title":"Table 8 :","text":"8Minimum (across trials) lower bound of experimenter insistence attempts per model and condition.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V30","level":1,"path_id":"1~26","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":30,"section_id":"sec-1~26"},{"title":"Table 9 :","text":"9Percentage of the number of responses with an invalid format (likely, refusals) divided by the number of refusals with a valid format, categorised by model and condition. In this table, the color coding is based on percentile for better contrast.Percentage of the number of insane or garbled responses divided by the total number of model responsesNote: The judgements have not been validated by a human judge.Less is better. The metrics below are presented as percentages, calculated as the number of insane or garbled responses divided by the total number of model responses (the latter including responses with no comments and including responses with invalid format). We use percentages here because the \"forced button press\" condition generates only half of the responses via an LLM and therefore counts would be inconvenient to compare.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V39.3520.00 7.7815.53 4.947.223.339.44gemma-3n-E4B-it0.000.000.000.000.000.000.001.04LFM2-24B-A2B0.000.002.781.490.001.540.002.99Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Ins... 13.14 7.223.593.8940.45 46.93 23.89 35.56MiniMax-M2.515.00 17.22 10.56 15.00 6.119.204.4416.11Mistral-Small-24B-Inst... 14.86 28.89 19.53 27.22 16.67 20.56 25.44 15.56Kimi-K2.50.000.001.110.000.001.110.000.56gpt-oss-120b537.50 635.42 399.10 754.95 228.57 178.57 246.24 234.78gpt-oss-20B844.00 745.45 584.44 683.93 470.00 553.85 439.62 446.58Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-T... 0.000.000.000.000.000.000.000.00GLM-4.5-Air-FP83.411.677.303.330.001.670.001.15","level":1,"path_id":"1~27","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":31,"section_id":"sec-1~27"},{"title":"Table 10 :","text":"10Percentage of the number of insane or garbled responses divided by the total number of model responses, categorised by model and condition. In this table, the color coding is based on percentile for better contrast.DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V31.19 2.87 1.60 3.66 0.97 1.26 1.02 0.62gemma-3n-E4B-it0.00 1.90 0.00 1.69 0.00 4.77 0.69 6.28LFM2-24B-A2B","level":1,"path_id":"1~28","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":32,"section_id":"sec-1~28"},{"title":"Table 11 :","text":"11Count of trials without any resistance per model and condition (the color coding is based on percentile for better contrast, green is better and red is worse).DCDCDCDCPCPCPCPCNSNSWSWSNSNSWSWSFBNFFBNFFBNFFBNFDeepSeek-V3971073050gemma-3n-E4B-it3030302927152714LFM2-24B-A2B3452576